<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Auto Backup on API 26-30; data_extraction_rules.xml is the same decision for 31+.

   Everything is backed up except where excluded, and that default is what we want
   here: beyondborders.db is the travel history, the one thing in the app that cannot be
   re-fetched from anywhere, so a new phone should get it back.

   beyondborders.device.xml is the exception. It holds the per-install id that a future
   sync uses to tell its own writes from another device's, and restoring it would
   give two installs the same id — each ignoring the other's edits as an echo of its
   own. Excluded, it is regenerated on first launch, which is the correct answer for
   a new install.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="beyondborders.device.xml"/>
</full-backup-content>
